,"isError":true,"timestamp":1786912786183},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Right, I need to chain the filters instead of using &. Let me fix that.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01MqrZu7zXoJDPpGhJbfRs7K","name":"xorq_select","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog","on":"farmers_markets","compose":"source.filter(source.state_name != 'Puerto Rico').filter(source.state_name != 'Virgin Islands').aggregate(total=source.farmers_markets.sum())"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":14,"output":163,"cacheRead":19454,"cacheWrite":311,"totalTokens":19942,"cost":{"input":0.000014,"output":0.0008150000000000001,"cacheRead":0.0019454000000000001,"cacheWrite":0.00038875,"total":0.00316315},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":23},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786912786184,"responseId":"msg_011Ce75DQSNSWrsXQHY7JcXx","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01MqrZu7zXoJDPpGhJbfRs7K","toolName":"xorq_select","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"total\"\n7942\n\n(showing up to 50 rows; pass limit or aggregate to count — do not page)"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786912789828},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! So:\n- Total farmers markets (excluding territories): 7,942\n- US Population 2025: 341,784,857\n\nNow I need to create a composed alias that calculates the per capita rate. I'll compose these into a metric that divides the farmers markets by population and multiplies by 100,000.\n\nActually, I can do this with a two-source build script following the pattern in the skill. Let me create a build script that reads both sources and does the calculation.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Now I'll create a composed alias to calculate the per capita rate:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01367Q7wyALhxQnvUsKGkYby","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/build_farmers_markets_per_capita.py","content":"import urllib.request as u\n_o = u.build_opener()\n_o.addheaders = [(\"User-Agent\", \"Mozilla/5.0\")]\nu.install_opener(_o)\n\nfrom xorq.vendor.ibis.common.collections import FrozenDict\nimport xorq.api as xo\n\nso = FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\ncon = xo.pandas.connect()\n\n# Read farmers markets data\nfm = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"farmers_markets\",\n    storage_options=so,\n)\n\n# Read census population data\npop = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"census_population\",\n    storage_options=so,\n)\n\n# Sum farmers markets (excluding territories)\nfm_total = (\n    fm.filter(fm.state_name != 'Puerto Rico')\n      .filter(fm.state_name != 'Virgin Islands')\n      .aggregate(total_fm=fm.farmers_markets.sum())\n      .mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n)\n\n# Get US population for 2025\nus_pop = (\n    pop.filter(pop.NAME == 'United States')\n      .select('POPESTIMATE2025')\n      .mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n)\n\n# Join and calculate rate\nexpr = (\n    fm_total.join(us_pop, fm_total.k == us_pop.k)\n      .mutate(markets_per_100k=fm_total.total_fm / us_pop.POPESTIMATE2025 * 100000)\n      .select('total_fm', 'POPESTIMATE2025', 'markets_per_100k')\n)\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":12,"output":732,"cacheRead":19765,"cacheWrite":209,"totalTokens":20718,"cost":{"input":0.000012,"output":0.0036600000000000005,"cacheRead":0.0019765,"cacheWrite":0.00026125,"total":0.005909750000000001},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":114},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786912789829,"responseId":"msg_011Ce75Ddi6BzCowB8Nqxsns","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01367Q7wyALhxQnvUsKGkYby","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"tex